@@ -449,6 +449,9 @@ The entries below give the details; the main cases are:
 
 #### Core, performance and input
 
+  - The virial of the collective variables that compute it from the atomic derivatives (e.g. [DISTANCE](DISTANCE.md), [GYRATION](GYRATION.md) and the multicolvars)
+    is computed about four times faster: the loop over the atoms stalled on a temporary tensor. With 20 [GYRATION](GYRATION.md) of 1000 atoms the forward loop is 20% faster,
+    with 200 [DISTANCE](DISTANCE.md) 10% faster. The results are identical.
   - The neighbor lists (e.g. [COORDINATION](COORDINATION.md) with `NLIST` and `NL_STRIDE` larger than one) build the list of the atoms that are needed
     by marking them instead of sorting the two atoms of every pair. With a [COORDINATION](COORDINATION.md) between 500 and 1500 atoms, `NL_CUTOFF=1.0` and
     `NL_STRIDE=10` (about 120000 pairs) the calculation is 33% faster. The results are identical.
